-first we setup our Arduino IDE. This involved installing the esp32 plugin. this was under tools->boards->board manager we found esp32espressif and installed that
-We then plugged in our ESP32 to our computer and in the IDE selected esp32-s3 dev module
-We then copied the code into the IDE and verified it before uploading it to the esp32
-We used the piserial library to read the data from the esp32 and print it to the screen
	-we had to import the serial library
	-than we created a serial object with the baud rate of the esp32 115200 and mounted it
	-lastly we could just read the data using data.read()
